-- erwartet: M109
-- **`&f` names a function, and one character took the name check away** (2026-09-02).
--
-- `m1::sammle_namen_pred` collects the names of an `ensures` so that `M109` can hold them
-- against the declarations. Its walker enumerated eight expression forms -- including
-- `sizeof`/`lenof`/`aligned`, which were added on 2026-08-21 for exactly this reason -- and
-- closed with `_ => {}`. **`ExprArt::FnWert` was not among them.**
--
--     ensures result == tippfehler     ->  M109  `tippfehler` … is not declared here
--     ensures result == &tippfehler    ->  0 errors
--
-- `FnWert(Pfad)` carries no sub-expression, so it looks like a leaf and fell in with the
-- leaves. *It is a leaf that NAMES something* -- and `M109` exists for exactly the names
-- nobody writes wrong: *"eine Nachbedingung, deren Namen nicht aufloesen, steht im Zeugnis
-- und in der Bibliotheks-ABI -- und sagt nichts."*
--
-- **The two forms resolve in different tables, and that is why the repair carries the `&`
-- into the collected name.** A bare name in value position is a PLACE (`ast.rs`, at
-- `FnWert`); with the `&` it is a FUNCTION. The bare form has to keep falling and the `&`
-- form has to resolve among functions -- one list of strings, two questions.
module gift::a_function_pointer_name_nobody_declares {

static mut Z : u32 = 0;

type Probe = fn() -> bool
    effects { reads Z }
    costs   <= 4 ops;

impl fn hart_bereit() -> bool
    effects { reads Z }
    costs   <= 3 ops
{
    return Z == 1;
}

impl fn baue() -> Probe
    ensures result == &tippfehler
    effects { pure }
    costs   <= 2 ops
{
    return &hart_bereit;
}

}
